iOS Keeps Observing a Dead Kotlin Flow — the CommonFlow Leak Hiding in Your KMP Bridge
So you've wrapped your shared Flow<T> for Swift consumption. Something like this on the Kotlin side:
class CommonFlow<T : Any>(private val wrapped: Flow<T>) {
    fun watch(block: (T) -> Unit): CommonFlowCancellation {
        val job = Job()
        wrapped.onEach {
            block(it)
        }.launchIn(CoroutineScope(Dispatchers.Main + job))
        return CommonFlowCancellation(job)
    }
}

class CommonFlowCancellation(private val job: Job) {
    fun cancel() {
        job.cancel()
    }
}

